/* BUSINESS DIRECTORY
   One business per line, in JSON format: keys and text in "double quotes", no trailing commas.
   Owners who have claimed their listing can also update their own line from their dashboard,
   so expect commits titled "Owner update: <slug>" in the history.

   slug:      the business's web address and stats ID, e.g. business/reliable-roofing/. Never change it.
   premium:   true = Premium listing (sits above Basic, gold border, shows about, hours, offer, gallery, ad image).
   postcard:  true = on the current Spotlight postcard ("On the Spotlight postcard" tag).
   claimed:   true = an owner has claimed it (set automatically when Todd approves a claim).
   blurb, phone, url, address:            Basic fields (owners can edit).
   about, hours, offer, gallery:          Premium fields (owners can edit). offer = {"title","details","expires":"YYYY-MM-DD"}.
   happyHour: text like "Every day, 3 to 6 PM". Puts the business in the Happy hours group and filter too (on top of its own category).
   features:  list of short labels shown as pills (dog parks: "Off-leash", "Fenced", "Small dog area", "Grass", "Shade", "Water for dogs", "Benches", "Restrooms", "Parking", "Lights", "Double gates", "Play features", "Walking path"). Only list what an official source confirms.
   size:      text like "About 1.6 acres" (shown on the profile). For courts, the court count, e.g. "8 courts"; it also shows on the directory card.
   courts:    pickleball and tennis only. {"setup","surface","nets","lights","play","levels","reserve","cost","lessons","closures","rules","note","contact","checked":"YYYY-MM-DD"}, all optional. Shown as a "Court details" card on the profile.
   trail:     hiking trails only. {"summary" (short line for the directory card, e.g. "1.8 mi loop · 350 ft · Strenuous"),"length","climb","difficulty","time","route","dogs","fee","hours","parking","facilities","shade","season","permit","guided","closures","rules","note","contact","checked":"YYYY-MM-DD"}, all optional. Shown as a "Trail details" card on the profile. Trail pills: "Free", "Fee", "Tram ticket", "Permit needed", "Dogs on leash", "No dogs", "Loop", "Out and back", "Paved", "Restrooms", "Water fountain", "Water refill", "Picnic tables", "Shade", "Little shade", "Waterfall", "Palm oasis", "Guided hikes", "Plant guide", "Views", "Cooler up top".
   public:    true = a public place (dog parks, hiking trails, public courts), not a business: no claim link and no "tell them you found them" line on its page.
   googlePlaceId: Premium only. The Google place ID; turns on the live Google reviews section on the profile.
   service:   the specific trade under the category, e.g. "Plumbing" under "Home services". Builds pages like local/palm-desert/plumbing/.
   name, category, service, city, image, area:     set by Todd only. */
